claim.claim-text:
a plurality of armatures associated with a plurality of phases of voltage signals, wherein each armature is configured to move between a respective first position that electrically couples a respective armature to respective first contact and a respective second position that electrically couples the respective armature to a respective second contact;
a plurality of coils, wherein each coil is configured to receive a respective voltage configured to magnetize a respective coil, thereby causing the respective armature to move from the respective first position to the respective second position;
a control system configured to:

receiving, via a processor, data associated with a change in current;
determining, via the processor, whether the change in current exceeds a threshold; and
sending, via the processor, a signal to an actuator coupled to a single-pole switching device in response to the change in current exceeding the threshold, wherein the signal is configured to cause the actuator to move a contact within the single-pole switching device.

wherein the actuator is configured to separate the contact from an additional contact within the single-pole switching device;
wherein the change in current is associated with a current exceeding a second threshold within a period of time;
wherein the threshold is determined based on a relationship between the contact and a change in current value that corresponds to the contact moving;
wherein the data comprises a detected fault; and
wherein the data comprises an inductance associated with the actuator.
